title: Shrine_LanternsDay
---
Five stone lanterns line the path from the gate to the hall.
The one by the gate is black with soot. Each one after it is a little cleaner, and the one by the hall is almost white.
<<flag clue_lantern_soot>>
===
title: Lantern_1
---
<<if met("flag:lanterns_lit")>>
The lantern by the gate burns steadily. Snow drips from its cap.
<<else>>
The lantern by the gate. Its stone is black with old soot.
Down the path, each lantern is cleaner than the one before it, from the black one by the gate to the almost white one by the hall.
<<flag clue_lantern_soot>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Lantern_2
---
<<if met("flag:lanterns_lit")>>
The second lantern burns steadily.
<<else>>
Dark grey with soot. Not quite as black as the one by the gate.
Down the path, each lantern is cleaner than the one before it, from the black one by the gate to the almost white one by the hall.
<<flag clue_lantern_soot>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Lantern_3
---
<<if met("flag:lanterns_lit")>>
The middle lantern burns steadily.
<<else>>
The middle lantern. A little soot, about half as much as the first.
Down the path, each lantern is cleaner than the one before it, from the black one by the gate to the almost white one by the hall.
<<flag clue_lantern_soot>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Lantern_4
---
<<if met("flag:lanterns_lit")>>
The fourth lantern burns steadily.
<<else>>
Only a faint ring of soot under the cap.
Down the path, each lantern is cleaner than the one before it, from the black one by the gate to the almost white one by the hall.
<<flag clue_lantern_soot>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Lantern_5
---
<<if met("flag:lanterns_lit")>>
The lantern by the hall burns steadily. Its stone looks new in the light.
<<else>>
The lantern by the hall. The stone is almost clean, as if it has hardly ever burned.
Down the path, each lantern is cleaner than the one before it, from the black one by the gate to the almost white one by the hall.
<<flag clue_lantern_soot>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Shrine_OfferingBox
---
<<if met("item:matchbox")>>
The offering box. Only snow in it now.
<<else>>
The offering box is full of snow. Under it, someone has left a box of matches. Dry, somehow.
<<give matchbox>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Lanterns_Gutter
---
The match flares. The flame curls away from the wick and dies.
===
title: Lanterns_Solved
---
The last lantern catches. Five flames burn in a row, from the gate to the hall.
Behind them, the snow slides off the hall doors with a soft hiss.
===
title: CloseUp_Nothing
---
Nothing happens.
===
title: Hall_Sealed
---
The hall doors are packed with snow, frozen as hard as stone.
Along the path behind you, the lanterns stand dark.
===
title: Tablet_Unreadable
---
A stone slab, taller than you, stands in the middle of the hall. Five signs are carved down its face.
The marks are old and strange. You can't read a single one.
Someone who has studied the old script could. Or a friend who has.
===
title: Tablet_Gate
---
Two posts and a beam, like the torii outside. Gate.
===
title: Tablet_Cold
---
Three strokes, each shorter than the last, like snow settling. Cold.
===
title: Tablet_Sleep
---
A closed eye. Sleep.
===
title: Tablet_Fire
---
Three flames, the middle one tallest. Fire.
===
title: Tablet_Wake
---
An open eye in a frame. Wake.
===
title: Tablet_Read
---
<<if met("knowledge >= 2")>>
The library books were good for something. The last sign gives itself up.
<<else>>
Aoi's notes fill in the last sign. She was right about "sleep".
<<endif>>
<<jump Tablet_Rule>>
===

title: Tablet_Rule
---
Read top to bottom, it is a rule, not a prayer.
Through the gate, into the cold, one sleeps. Only a fire wakes the sleeper.
<<flag clue_tablet>>
===
